2 CONT Horrifying Tragedy At Farm Home Near FlandreauSaturday morning about 6:00 o'clock Mrs. Lloyd Orvedahl killed her three children. She then went out to the barn where her husband was doing chores and told him what she had done, Sayi
2 CONC ng, "It's all right. They'll go to heaven now."Mrs. Orvedahl had been suffering from a nervous breakdown, and it is said at one time told her husband that she was going insane and asked him to send her to the asylum. She had been 
2 CONC worrying about the future of her children, caused by the breakdown.The Orvedahl farm, where the tragedy occurred, is about eight miles south of Flandreau. The children were aged 3, 7, and 9 years.Mrs. Orvedahl was highly respected
2 CONC  by her friends and neighbors, a Christian, well educated, and above the average in intelligence.Mr. Orvedahl took his wife to Flandreau and there she was placed in jail for a few hours and then she was taken to Yankton and placed
2 CONC  in the state hospital.It is a terrible tragedy and comes home to the people of this community, as Mrs. Orvedahl is the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. A.L. Brendsel of near Baltic, and a niece of L.K. Larson. She has a great many friend
2 CONC s here.Dell Rapids Tribune April 28, 1927
