1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT After a few years in town, Orin spent most of his life on a farm in Blinsmon Township. Orins elementary education was received in a rural school, Blinsmon #9. After graduation he entered Flandreau High School in 1934 but took his
2 CONC  second and third years of high school at Egan Consolidated School. He completed his high school education at Augustana College but preferred to be working outdoors on the farm.Orin was inducted into the Army in late January of 19
2 CONC 43. Enrolled in the 86th Reconnaissance Troop of the Mechanized Cavalry, he took his training at Camp Howze, Texas; Camp Livingston, Louisiana; Camp Crook and Camp San Luis Obispo in California. Orin received the highest score in 
2 CONC the whole troop at the rifle range and was classified as an expert.Sgt. Orin Amdahl sailed for overseas service in February of 1945 and was killed in action April 14, 1945, in Germany, later identified as in the city of Hagen.The 
2 CONC letter that Sgt. Amdahls captain wrote to Orins mother stated in part:On the 14th of April your son was concerned to fulfill his assigned task according to the best American tradition. He and other men of his platoon had the res
2 CONC ponsibilityof clearing out a hostile position which was greatly hindering the progress of ourtroops. His death occurred instantly as the result of a shell fragment wound. He received a Christian burial in the American Military Cem
2 CONC etery in Breuna, Germany,16th April 1945.
