1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Ur minnesrunan vid Lowells bortgång: Lowell worked on the family farm in South Dakota before joining the U.S. Army. He then attended South Dakota State University where he received his B.S. degree in Physics. He continued his educ
2 CONC ation at the University of Kansas where he then earned his Masters Degree in Physics. While in Kansas, Lowell also worked in a box factory and the printing department at the local newspaper.His first job after receiving his Maste
2 CONC rs Degree was with IBM in New York City. He then moved his family to Redondo Beach in California where he started work at Ramo Wooldridge (later known as TRW). The family then relocated to Northridge (where Lowell and Iva lived i
2 CONC n same beautiful home for 55 years) and Lowell later became president of a new consulting firm -- Digital Science Consultants. His next career path included starting Amdahl Associates which later became Compata, Inc. with his fina
2 CONC l employment being with Computer Science Corporation (CSC). Lowell also taught computer classes at night at both UCLA and USC and he then served as Technical Editor for Datamation magazine for 15 years.Lowell very much enjoyed tra
2 CONC velling both prior to and following his retirement in 1991. These trips included: An adventure to Europe in 1970 with Iva and teenage children Paul, Joan and Rob; a trip with Iva and friends to Norway in 1973; and an RV road trip 
2 CONC to Alaska, Canada and South Dakota with Iva, grandson Jason and some RV and square dancing friends in 1983. Lowell and Iva then participated in group tours to Italy, The Holy Land and Greece in 1988, an Orient Cruise in 1995 and t
2 CONC rip to Eastern Europe in 2000.Lowell enjoyed time with friends and family RVing, square dancing, playing golf and tennis and playing a variety of card games and working on puzzles. Lowell was also very much a man of faith and was 
2 CONC very involved with the First Lutheran Church of Northridge (now Lifehouse Church).All who knew Lowell would agree that he had an amazing knack for humorous wit and was a man of the highest integrity while remaining a humble gentle
2 CONC man.
