1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?db=1940usfedcen&indiv=try&h=109967510
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/search/record/results?count=20&query=%2Bgivenname%3ALoren~%20%2Bsurname%3AHesla~
2 CONT
2 CONT http://obituaries.tylerpaper.com/obituaries/tylerpaper/obituary.aspx?page=lifestory&pid=186728080
2 CONT
2 CONT Loren Neil Hesla passed away September 20, 2017. Loren was born March 14, 1929, in Wakonda, SD, to Inman A. Hesla and Agnes B. Hesla. He was raised on a farm in Wakonda, the youngest of five children who have all preceded him in d
2 CONC eath. He attended Augustana University in Sioux Falls, SD, then moved to Dallas and graduated from SMU. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He met and married his first wife, Freida Rose Jackson Dillon while she was attending Baylor Nursing School. Together they had three children, Joy Rose, Jeffrey Loren, Jennifer Leigh and remained married for 58 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his first wife, Loren met and married Iris Freeman from Corsicana. They have been married for eight years and have continued to reside at Hideaway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Loren worked in sales for most of his career selling commercial furniture for American Hospital Supplies and Thonet while living in Dallas. Loren and Freida moved to Hideaway Lake in 1982 where they started a residential real esta
2 CONC te business, Crown Realty specializing in HAWL properties. They eventually retired and sold the company.
2 CONT
2 CONT Loren loved to sing and had a beautiful baritone voice which he shared while singing in many choirs and performing solos. Loren and his family were founding members of King of Glory Lutheran Church in Dallas where he served in wha
2 CONC tever capacity needed, whether council member, elder, janitor or choir member. He loved playing bridge with his friends at Hideaway, enjoyed Sudoko and the daily crossword puzzle.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is currently a member of Our Saviour's Lutheran Church in Tyler. He and Iris also enjoyed attending Green Acres Baptist Church where Iris is a member. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Loren was preceded in death by his parents, four siblings and first wife Freida. He is survived by his loving wife of eight years Iris Freemen Hesla; her children, Phil and Teri; grandchildren and great-grandchildren. He is also s
2 CONC urvived by his children, Joy Gissler and husband Jim, Jeff Hesla and wife Toni, Jenny Biernacki and husband Rick and grandchildren, Josh, Heidi, Loren Paige, Samantha and their families, including his great-grandchildren, Pierce, 
2 CONC Emma and Benton along with many nieces, nephews, step grand and great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those who knew Loren are comforted that He is at Home with His Lord and Savior, Jesus Christ. He will be greatly missed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held at Our Saviour's Lutheran Church, 4900 Kinsey Drive, Tyler, 75703, Saturday, September 23, 2017, at 2 p.m. with reception to follow. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers donations may be made in Loren's memory to The Hospice of East Texas Foundation, Tyler, 75701.
