1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Herbert S. Peterson was born on April 7, 1919 in Volga, South Dakota the son of Karl and Lava (Brendsel) Peterson. He died on Friday, October 24, 2003 at the Brookings Hospital at the age of 84 years. Herbert gradu
2 CONC ated from Baltic High School in 1938. He served in WWII from January 1942 to January 1946 on the West Coast and in Europe-England and France. He was a staff sergeant with the 1272nd Combat Engineers. He was united in marriage to L
2 CONC eona Jennings on June 20, 1954 in Brookings, SD. They made their home in Brookings. He was employed with his brother Leonard at Midway Grocery from 1954 until 1970 and then at the Trading Post in Brookings from 1972 until 2002. He
2 CONC  was a member of the Mt. Calvary Lutheran Church and the American Legion. He was a fan of local high school and college sports as well as the Minnesota Twins and Vikings. He especially enjoyed spending time with family and friends
2 CONC . Herbert is survived by his wife Leona of Brookings; one son Mark Peterson and his wife Marilyn of Ogden, Utah; one daughter Joan Fink and her husband Randy of Sioux Falls, SD; grandchildren Nathan Shivers and his wife Jane, Eric
2 CONC , Marta and Jackson Fink; two great-grandchildren Haley and Max Shivers; one brother Leonard Peterson and his wife Verna of Brookings, SD; one sister Nellie Poll and her husband Dwain of Aurora, CO; brothers-in-law and sisters-in-
2 CONC law Bob and Irene Loch, Rich and Connie Jennings, George and Evelyn Dunlap, Clarice and Mark Wiese, Jim and Hester Jennings, Pernie and Peggy Jennings, Kathy Jennings and many nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by his pa
2 CONC rents, an infant daughter and one sister (Mildred) and brother-in-law (Glen Jennings). http://www.rudesfuneralhome.com/memsol.cgi?user_id=341599
