1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=28228658 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:  Dec. 3, 1919 Rice County Minnesota, USA  Death:  Jul. 10, 2008 Cannon Falls Goodhue County Minnesota, USA  Edwin Gerhard Fredrickson, age 88, of rural Northfield, died on Thursday, July 10, 2008, at the Angels Care Center,
2 CONC  Cannon Falls, following a short illness. Edwin was born on Dec. 3, 1919, to Oscar and Hilma Frederickson. He lived his entire life on the farm where he was born, which has been in his family since the 1860s and was designated as 
2 CONC a Minnesota Century Farm. Edwin was a veteran of World War II, stationed in the Mediterranean theater. He returned to the Farmington/Northfield area and worked for the Dakota County Highway Department for 32 years. Edwin married H
2 CONC elen Jensen on March 28, 1946. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edwin was a life member of the VFW Post 210 in Lakeville, Minn. In his retirement he enjoyed his family, old cars, John Deere tractors, gardening and bird watching. He loved to tell stories about the "good old days." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edwin is survived by his daughters, Edith (Verlin) Wirth of Apple Valley, Minn., and Sally (Daryl) Robinson of rural Northfield; grandson, Daniel (Toni) Fredrickson of Farmington; one great-grandson, Jack Fredrickson; and by many 
2 CONC nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by his wife, Helen; sisters, Evelyn Vick, Elizabeth Henry and Alma Hammersten, from the area; and two brothers and three sisters from Norway. 
